WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.950
Polite Requests and Offers.

2
00:00:02.230 --> 00:00:05.686
Day 9 of the Soft Skill Playbook course, in the English phase.

3
00:00:07.436 --> 00:00:08.460
The key idea.

4
00:00:08.740 --> 00:00:13.540
Today's goal: ask for things, offer help, ask permission and refuse, politely.

5
00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:18.108
The same words sound rude or kind depending on how you build the sentence.

6
00:00:19.458 --> 00:00:20.311
Part 1.

7
00:00:20.591 --> 00:00:21.871
The politeness ladder.

8
00:00:23.121 --> 00:00:25.361
Give me the bill.: an order; sounds rude.

9
00:00:25.641 --> 00:00:28.969
Can I have the bill?: fine with friends, shops, cafés.

10
00:00:29.249 --> 00:00:32.961
Could I have the bill, please?: polite: use this as your default.

11
00:00:33.241 --> 00:00:35.759
Would you mind bringing the bill?: very polite.

12
00:00:36.039 --> 00:00:40.689
I was wondering if you could...: very formal; for big requests and senior people.

13
00:00:42.039 --> 00:00:42.914
Part 2.

14
00:00:43.194 --> 00:00:45.626
Requests: asking someone to do something.

15
00:00:46.876 --> 00:00:48.241
Here is a quick table:

16
00:00:48.521 --> 00:00:49.887
Pattern, and Example.

17
00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.404
Can you + verb...?:

18
00:00:51.684 --> 00:00:52.985
Can you send me the link?

19
00:00:53.265 --> 00:00:55.100
Could you + verb... please?:

20
00:00:55.380 --> 00:00:57.193
Could you speak a bit slower, please?

21
00:00:57.473 --> 00:00:58.753
Would you + verb...?:

22
00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:00.377
Would you check this for me?

23
00:01:00.657 --> 00:01:02.279
Would you mind + verb-ing...?:

24
00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:04.308
Would you mind closing the window?

25
00:01:04.588 --> 00:01:05.868
Do you think you could...?:

26
00:01:06.148 --> 00:01:08.388
Do you think you could review my PR today?

27
00:01:09.738 --> 00:01:11.210
Answering Would you mind...?:

28
00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:14.093
No, not at all. = Yes, I'll do it!

29
00:01:14.373 --> 00:01:16.229
(because mind = object).

30
00:01:17.579 --> 00:01:18.475
Part 3.

31
00:01:18.755 --> 00:01:19.949
Asking for things.

32
00:01:21.199 --> 00:01:23.034
Could I have a glass of water, please?

33
00:01:23.314 --> 00:01:26.151
I'd like (= I would like) a window seat, please.

34
00:01:26.431 --> 00:01:28.330
Can I get a medium cappuccino?

35
00:01:28.610 --> 00:01:29.549
(cafés).

36
00:01:29.829 --> 00:01:31.258
Do you have this in black?

37
00:01:32.608 --> 00:01:33.525
Part 4.

38
00:01:33.805 --> 00:01:35.021
Asking permission.

39
00:01:36.271 --> 00:01:37.637
Here is a quick table:

40
00:01:37.917 --> 00:01:39.943
Pattern, and Example, and Reply.

41
00:01:40.223 --> 00:01:41.077
Can I...?

42
00:01:41.357 --> 00:01:42.231
Example:

43
00:01:42.511 --> 00:01:43.578
Can I sit here?

44
00:01:43.858 --> 00:01:44.711
Reply:

45
00:01:44.991 --> 00:01:46.485
Sure. / Go ahead.

46
00:01:46.765 --> 00:01:47.618
Could I...?

47
00:01:47.898 --> 00:01:48.773
Example:

48
00:01:49.053 --> 00:01:51.079
Could I leave 30 minutes early today?

49
00:01:51.359 --> 00:01:52.213
Reply:

50
00:01:52.493 --> 00:01:53.687
Yes, that's fine.

51
00:01:53.967 --> 00:01:54.842
May I...?

52
00:01:55.122 --> 00:01:55.890
(formal).

53
00:01:56.170 --> 00:01:57.045
Example:

54
00:01:57.325 --> 00:01:58.370
May I come in?

55
00:01:58.650 --> 00:01:59.503
Reply:

56
00:01:59.783 --> 00:02:00.701
Please do.

57
00:02:00.981 --> 00:02:02.303
Is it okay if I...?

58
00:02:02.583 --> 00:02:03.458
Example:

59
00:02:03.738 --> 00:02:05.658
Is it okay if I join by phone?

60
00:02:05.938 --> 00:02:06.791
Reply:

61
00:02:07.071 --> 00:02:07.967
Of course.

62
00:02:08.247 --> 00:02:09.442
Do you mind if I...?

63
00:02:09.722 --> 00:02:10.597
Example:

64
00:02:10.877 --> 00:02:12.669
Do you mind if I open the window?

65
00:02:12.949 --> 00:02:13.802
Reply:

66
00:02:14.082 --> 00:02:15.106
No, go ahead.

67
00:02:16.456 --> 00:02:17.416
Part 5.

68
00:02:17.696 --> 00:02:19.232
Offers and suggestions.

69
00:02:20.482 --> 00:02:21.911
Shall I call a cab for you?

70
00:02:22.191 --> 00:02:25.605
Would you like some tea? then Yes, please. / No, thank you.

71
00:02:25.885 --> 00:02:27.399
Can I help you with that bag?

72
00:02:27.679 --> 00:02:30.325
Let me help you. / Let me check that for you.

73
00:02:30.605 --> 00:02:35.362
Why don't we take a break? / How about meeting on Monday? / Let's order lunch.

74
00:02:36.712 --> 00:02:37.651
Part 6.

75
00:02:37.931 --> 00:02:39.253
Refusing politely.

76
00:02:40.503 --> 00:02:42.637
I'm sorry, I'm afraid I can't today.

77
00:02:42.917 --> 00:02:45.519
Thanks for asking, but I have another commitment.

78
00:02:45.799 --> 00:02:48.082
I'd love to, but I'm travelling that week.

79
00:02:48.362 --> 00:02:50.495
Unfortunately, that's not possible.

80
00:02:50.775 --> 00:02:52.013
What I can do is...

81
00:02:53.363 --> 00:02:54.301
Part 7.

82
00:02:54.581 --> 00:02:56.160
Magic words and phrases.

83
00:02:57.410 --> 00:02:58.775
Here is a quick table:

84
00:02:59.055 --> 00:03:00.165
Instead of, and Say.

85
00:03:00.445 --> 00:03:01.127
What?:

86
00:03:01.407 --> 00:03:04.693
Sorry? / Pardon? / Sorry, could you repeat that?

87
00:03:04.973 --> 00:03:05.698
Wait.:

88
00:03:05.978 --> 00:03:08.901
Just a moment, please. / Could you give me a minute?

89
00:03:09.181 --> 00:03:10.055
I want...:

90
00:03:10.335 --> 00:03:11.210
I'd like...

91
00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:12.215
Give...:

92
00:03:12.495 --> 00:03:14.650
Could you pass... / Could I have...

93
00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:15.655
Move.:

94
00:03:15.935 --> 00:03:17.663
Excuse me, could I get past?

95
00:03:17.943 --> 00:03:18.711
Tell me.:

96
00:03:18.991 --> 00:03:20.165
Could you let me know...?

97
00:03:20.445 --> 00:03:22.151
No problem (after thanks):

98
00:03:22.431 --> 00:03:25.631
You're welcome. / My pleasure. / Happy to help.

99
00:03:26.981 --> 00:03:27.856
Part 8.

100
00:03:28.136 --> 00:03:30.675
Conversation: asking a colleague for help.

101
00:03:31.925 --> 00:03:33.951
Here is how the conversation goes.

102
00:03:34.231 --> 00:03:36.109
Hi Meena, do you have a minute?

103
00:03:36.389 --> 00:03:37.583
Sure, what's up?

104
00:03:37.863 --> 00:03:41.725
I was wondering if you could help me with the Kafka configuration.

105
00:03:42.005 --> 00:03:43.306
I'm a bit stuck.

106
00:03:43.586 --> 00:03:44.503
Of course.

107
00:03:44.783 --> 00:03:46.810
Would you mind waiting until 3?

108
00:03:47.090 --> 00:03:48.583
I'm in a meeting till then.

109
00:03:48.863 --> 00:03:50.058
Not at all.

110
00:03:50.338 --> 00:03:52.898
Shall I send you the error log before that?

111
00:03:54.248 --> 00:03:55.848
The conversation continues.

112
00:03:56.128 --> 00:03:57.237
Yes, please.

113
00:03:57.517 --> 00:03:58.541
That would help.

114
00:03:58.821 --> 00:04:00.379
Great, I'll send it now.

115
00:04:00.659 --> 00:04:03.475
And is it okay if I share my screen when we talk?

116
00:04:03.755 --> 00:04:04.885
Absolutely.

117
00:04:05.165 --> 00:04:07.853
Thanks so much, I really appreciate it.

118
00:04:08.133 --> 00:04:09.328
Happy to help!

119
00:04:10.678 --> 00:04:11.574
Part 9.

120
00:04:11.854 --> 00:04:12.771
Practice.

121
00:04:14.021 --> 00:04:14.661
1.

122
00:04:14.941 --> 00:04:16.072
Make these polite.

123
00:04:16.352 --> 00:04:17.440
Give me the menu.

124
00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:18.424
2.

125
00:04:18.704 --> 00:04:19.707
Repeat that.

126
00:04:19.987 --> 00:04:20.733
3.

127
00:04:21.013 --> 00:04:22.528
I want to change my seat.

128
00:04:22.808 --> 00:04:23.512
4.

129
00:04:23.792 --> 00:04:24.645
Wait here.

130
00:04:25.995 --> 00:04:26.913
Success:

131
00:04:27.193 --> 00:04:28.046
Answers.

132
00:04:28.326 --> 00:04:29.841
Could I have the menu, please?

133
00:04:30.121 --> 00:04:30.825
2.

134
00:04:31.105 --> 00:04:32.982
Sorry, could you repeat that, please?

135
00:04:33.262 --> 00:04:34.009
3.

136
00:04:34.289 --> 00:04:36.827
I'd like to change my. seat, if possible.

137
00:04:37.107 --> 00:04:37.811
4.

138
00:04:38.091 --> 00:04:39.883
Could you wait here for a moment, please?

139
00:04:41.233 --> 00:04:41.937
2.

140
00:04:42.217 --> 00:04:43.071
Reply.

141
00:04:43.351 --> 00:04:45.164
Would you mind turning off your phone?

142
00:04:45.444 --> 00:04:47.769
(You agree.) / Would you like some coffee?

143
00:04:48.049 --> 00:04:49.159
(You don't want it.).

144
00:04:50.509 --> 00:04:51.426
Success:

145
00:04:51.706 --> 00:04:52.559
Answers.

146
00:04:52.839 --> 00:04:53.991
No, not at all.

147
00:04:54.271 --> 00:04:56.362
(and turn it off) / No, thank you.

148
00:04:56.642 --> 00:04:57.495
I'm fine.

149
00:04:58.845 --> 00:04:59.592
3.

150
00:04:59.872 --> 00:05:01.109
Refuse politely.

151
00:05:01.389 --> 00:05:04.696
Your colleague asks you to stay late tonight to test their feature.

152
00:05:06.046 --> 00:05:06.963
Success:

153
00:05:07.243 --> 00:05:08.331
Sample answer.

154
00:05:08.611 --> 00:05:11.214
I'd love to help, but I can't stay late tonight.

155
00:05:11.494 --> 00:05:13.713
I could test it first thing tomorrow morning.

156
00:05:13.993 --> 00:05:14.974
Would that work?

157
00:05:16.324 --> 00:05:17.177
Part 10.

158
00:05:17.457 --> 00:05:18.503
Speak today.

159
00:05:19.753 --> 00:05:22.825
Use Could I...? or Could you...? at least 5 times.

160
00:05:23.105 --> 00:05:26.027
Replace one What? with Sorry, could you repeat that?

161
00:05:26.307 --> 00:05:28.953
Offer help once with Shall I...? or Let me...

162
00:05:30.303 --> 00:05:31.839
That's the end of this lesson.

163
00:05:32.119 --> 00:05:36.791
Pick one script from it, say it out loud three times, and use it for real today.

164
00:05:37.071 --> 00:05:43.172
For extra practice, paste the Master Prompt into an AI assistant and role-play the conversation.

